# Delvers S3E02 — Call your Mummy

**Identity:** Played **Delvers Season Three Episode Two — Call your Mummy**. Opening host dates this recording **Saturday, 2021-08-14**; **publisher release date not independently checked**. Immediate sequel to [S3E01](S3E01.md). **Unlike the prior premiere, this episode ACTUALLY plays and concludes the GM's approximately THREE-MONTH time passage**, starting with Evelyn's five-day trip home, daily cures and farm work, and ending with a new public dungeon-raid regime at Atomer.

**ACTUAL PLAYED CUTOFF (~02:51:50):** About **three in-world months after the Bronze Ball**, the city has become an advertised **Silver League dungeon-raiding hub**. Its walled financial district is under guild control and a public announcer sets new rules: arriving Silvers require an **inspection and an Atomer questing licence**; elves/half-elves/Sylvan descent must stay outside governor's square; **no overnight tunnel stays**; consult the guild for raids at boss doors/monster nests. These are **announced rules, not yet performed Delvers registration or expedition**. Evelyn's parents **finally recognize her as a paladin**, abandon the Julian Thomas arrangement as their requirement, and she **actually returns to Atomer astride a newly summoned celestial elk**. Koh now resides in a smaller **purchased home near the guild**, supports family with a **paid stipend as feral-elf hunter**, carries Carrie's **red-crystal detection amulet upgraded with a directional indicator**, and is **still officially grounded from regular guild quests**. Krandal's potato farm expands, a **3,500-gp barn is actually built**, he defeats and **kills** a surgically hollowed-out apparent elf mummy/assassin bearing Khalazar's bat symbol, and continues farming. Cassius's investigation remains unresolved; **no conviction, release or rescue from custody shown**. Neither the public claim that Khalazar was driven underground nor the guild's advertisement proves Khalazar slain or the Hereditary Drone destroyed.

**Evidence:** [P SRT](../../sources/Delvers%20S3E02.%20Call%20your%20Mummy.parakeet.processed.srt) · [Q8 SRT](../../sources/Delvers%20S3E02.%20Call%20your%20Mummy.qwen-q8.canary-ctc.nemotron.srt) · [ASR comparison and source limitations](../../reports/DELVERS_S3E02_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) · [queue](../REVIEW_QUEUE.md). All Parakeet primary text read through final FrogPants ident, Qwen Q8 complete for metric and selected independently reviewed high-risk clock windows. Both files fetched from **GitHub current default branch**, blob identities below. Initial local workspace at `2e82c5bacffa26ce23e6ce7e28290134fe940108`, with **four pre-existing unrelated illustration-skill edits**; GitHub could not resolve this local commit (404). Local P beginning/end and Q beginning match fetched versions, **complete byte-for-byte local/remote equivalence not proven**. No MP3 audio, original GM farm map, shared spell handouts or published metadata verified. **ASR-PROVISIONAL throughout.**

